<title>UK: British Steel up, Vickers off.</title>
<headline>British Steel up, Vickers off.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering stocks had mixed fortunes on Friday after analysts at HSBC James Capel reviewed the sector, picking out British Steel as one their favourites ahead of results next week.</p>
<p>Sources said analysts at HSBC James Capel put &quot;buy&quot; recommendations on Weir Group, Laird Group and British Steel. Vickers and Rolls Royce were rated &quot;sell&quot;.</p>
<p>British Steel shares were up 2-3/4p at 169-3/4p by 1430 GMT after reaching 172p earlier. The shares pared gains after British Steel unit Avesta Sheffield reported first half profits had been almost wiped out by low prices and inventory losses.</p>
</text>
